---
import ContentPageLayout from '@/layouts/ContentPageLayout.astro'
import { REPOSITORY_URL } from '@/config/site'
---

<ContentPageLayout title="About Envarium" eyebrow="About the project" description="Start local services, read their logs, and track ports and project status from one application. Envarium is open source under Apache-2.0 and requires no Envarium account.">
  <section class="story"><div><p class="eyebrow">Why it exists</p><h2>See what is running.</h2></div><div><p>Keep a repository’s start commands, Compose services, ports, health checks, and logs together. Inspect a failed service, find a port conflict, or open a project terminal without collecting that information from separate tools.</p><p>The desktop app, browser interface, CLI, and MCP tools connect to the same local Go service. They share project definitions and operation history.</p></div></section>
  <section class="values"><article class="panel"><h2>No required cloud account</h2><p>Envarium stores project state locally. Your workloads and optional integrations may use the network; review those connections in the privacy guide.</p><a href="/privacy/">Data and optional connections →</a></article><article class="panel"><h2>Works without AI</h2><p>Discover projects, manage services, and inspect failures without an AI provider. Optional AI assistance uses evidence you review, and generated configuration requires human approval.</p><a href="/features/agents-mcp/">Coding-agent access →</a></article><article class="panel"><h2>Source you can inspect</h2><p>Read the code, build it yourself, and review the documented APIs and architecture decisions. Contributions use the same published repository guidelines.</p><a href="/contributing/">Build and contribute →</a></article></section>
  <p class="availability">Use Envarium on macOS or Linux. <a href="/download/">Check installation options</a>; Windows and WSL2 support is coming soon.</p>
  <aside class="credit panel"><div><strong>Created by David Cuellar.</strong><span>Repository history records code and documentation contributions. The license and notices are included with the source.</span></div><a class="button primary" href={REPOSITORY_URL}>Explore the source</a><a class="button" href={`${REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/master/NOTICE`}>Attributions</a><a class="button" href="/contributing/">Contribute</a></aside>
</ContentPageLayout>

<style>
  .story { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; gap: 3rem; }
  .story h2 { max-width: 10ch; margin: 0.4rem 0; font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 5rem); line-height: 0.98; }
  .story > div:last-child { color: var(--sy-text-muted); font-size: 1.06rem; }
  .values { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 0.8rem; margin-top: 5rem; }
  .values article { padding: 1.4rem; }
  .values p, .credit span { color: var(--sy-text-muted); }
  .values a, .availability a { color: var(--sy-accent-primary); font-weight: 760; }
  .availability { margin-top: 2rem; color: var(--sy-text-muted); }
  .credit { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 3rem; padding: 1.2rem; }
  .credit div { display: grid; margin-right: auto; }
  .credit > a { flex-shrink: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .story, .values { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .credit { align-items: stretch; flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
